tasks.description:
The folder and its rules, before anything moves into it — so the first extraction has something to be correct against.

## What exists

Nothing. App-level composition lives in `heca/src/chrome/mod.rs` (4960 lines) and inside providers. `heca/src/main.rs` declares the module list (`mod actions; mod app; mod chrome; …`) — `mod components;` joins it there.

## What to build

`heca/src/components/mod.rs` whose module doc states the contract that the project `globalRules` and AGENTS § 0b define, in the terms of this codebase:

- what may live here (composes widgets **and** binds an app concept: `Intent`, an action **name**, a drag id, a hint target id, a chrome signal, a `nav_key`) versus what belongs in `heca-grid-ui`;
- the signature rule: plain data + the seams (`Intent` / `ChromeIntentEmitter`, `&mut BuildCx`, an action name, `&GuiTheme`) and **never `&AppState`** — it needs a window, so it cannot exist in a test;
- what a component returns: a `Component` / `WidgetModel` built from library widgets — no `paint`, no measure, no hit-test, no scroll offset;
- the test rule: one headless test per component.

Nothing else in this task. An empty folder with a written contract is the point; the proof follows in the next task.

## Edge cases

- `main.rs` is a binary crate — the module must be reachable from `chrome/` and `providers/` (both already `crate::`-rooted), so plain `pub(crate)` items are enough; nothing here is part of a public API.
- Do **not** create a `components/` module inside `heca-grid-ui`. The library's own compositions (`Dialog`, `Select`, `CommandPalette`) are widgets and stay where they are.

---
**Completion summary:**
**Done 2026-08-12** (uncommitted, on `feat/palette-modes`).

`heca/src/components/mod.rs` created — module doc only, no items, which is the point: the folder plus the written contract, before anything moves into it. `mod components;` added to `heca/src/main.rs:5`. `cargo check -p heca` clean.

The doc states, in this codebase's terms:
- **what belongs here vs `heca-grid-ui`** — a composition that also binds an app concept (`Intent`, an action name, a drag id, a chrome signal, a `nav_key`); one that binds none of them is a widget in the wrong crate;
- **where a component lives** — beside its surface (`heca/src/chrome/<surface>/`) until a SECOND surface wants it; the second caller is the move, and it is a move, never a copy (Antonio, 2026-08-12; AGENTS § 0b carries the same qualification);
- **the signature rule** — plain data plus the seams it binds, **never `&AppState`**;
- **what it returns** — a component built from library widgets; no paint, measure, hit-test or scroll offset;
- **sizes are shares, never computed pixels** — `Length::Pct` of a shared denominator or a `grow` weight, with the exposé's seven attempts as the worked cost;
- **the test rule** — one headless test per component, following `providers/mod.rs::the_shared_context_carries_nothing_of_one_components_domain` or `heca-grid-ui/tests/phase_a.rs`, plus "lay it out in a box and assert it never exceeds it" for anything sized by shares.

Deliberately NOT written into it: the deleted hint API (`hints.register` / `.hint_target`) that the F011 and P087 descriptions still cited. Both of those descriptions were corrected in the same session.
